{
  "_comment": "Shape reference for Form 7a — a hook registration in .claude/settings.json, or in project-bootstrap/templates/settings.json.example for the generated project. MERGE into the `hooks` block that is already there; never replace it. Fields, events, and which events read a `matcher`: ../references/hook-events.md. Owner of the lists: .claude/schemas/extensions.json › settings.",

  "hooks": {
    "PreToolUse": [
      {
        "_comment": "matcher = tool name, or a list (Edit|Write), or a regex. Group level: only `matcher` and `hooks` exist here.",
        "matcher": "Write",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "_comment": "Shell form, one shape, no `args`: the GitHub Copilot CLI reads this same file, runs `command` alone and ignores `args`, so an exec-form entry exits 1 there and denies every call. Keep the placeholder braced and double-quoted: Claude Code substitutes it before the shell runs, a Unix shell under Copilot expands it from the environment. A pipe, &&, redirect or substitution inside `command` is rejected by `ArchHook.java schema`, and so is an `args` list. Design: .claude/decisions/0168-hooks-in-shell-form.md. Launch the precompiled jar, never the source: a source launch recompiles the whole hook on every call (~3 s against ~0.3 s). A new or changed mode means `java .claude/hooks/ArchHook.java build` and committing the jar — `schema` fails on a stale one. Path rules in `if` match only through `Edit(...)`, which covers Write too — `Write(...)` there never matches. Design: .claude/decisions/0075-precompiled-hook-jar.md.",
            "type": "command",
            "if": "Edit(<path glob the check actually concerns>)",
            "command": "java -jar \"${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR}/.claude/hooks/ArchHook.jar\" <mode>",
            "statusMessage": "<what the user sees while it runs>",
            "timeout": 30
          }
        ]
      }
    ],

    "Stop": [
      {
        "_comment": "No `matcher` here: Stop does not read one, and `ArchHook.java schema` rejects it. An event with no matcher and no `if` runs every single time — that is criterion 9 of the rubric, and it is only correct when the check genuinely has to.",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "java -jar \"${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR}/.claude/hooks/ArchHook.jar\" <mode>",
            "statusMessage": "<what the user sees while it runs>",
            "timeout": 60
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },

  "_comment_permissions": "Form 8 lives in the same file. `deny` is read before the call and spawns no process — prefer it over a hook whenever the answer is a flat refusal. Every line needs a reason in the decision record: there is nowhere here to write one.",
  "permissions": {
    "allow": ["Bash(<command that should never need approval>:*)"],
    "deny": ["Read(./**/<path that must never be read>)"]
  },

  "_comment_restart": "Nothing in this file takes effect until `claude` is restarted. It is read at session startup only."
}
